I'm playing nh3pl9 both at home on my XT clone (PC-DOS) and at work on a
Interactive 386/ix System V.3 system. Both places I've encountered the
same bug.

While wandering through a bones level I encountered one of my own
ghosts from a previous game (a priest). I found all the late priests
goodies, but in the pile there were "65533 black knives" (PC-version).

The same error in the UNIX version resulted in an equally large 32-bit
number (can't remember exactly) of black knives. I suppose this is due
to some wrap around or signed/unsigned problem.

Anyway, I didn't try to pick up the knives (wouldn't try to destroy a
promising game), but when trying to leave the level the program
chrashed on me. The worst thing was, that this happened *every* time
I went down to that level. I had to delete the bones files, to get
rid of the problem.

BTW, the PC version I play is not the "official" version, its compiled by
a friend of mine.


I'm mailing this to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu as well.

